# Full tests before push

Before **any** `git push` (including after commit when the user asked to push):

1. Run the **full** test suite: `npm test -- --no-coverage` (not only path-filtered suites).
2. Push **only if** all suites pass.
3. If tests fail, fix failures (or report them) and do **not** push until green.
4. In the reply after a push, briefly confirm that the full suite was run and passed (counts if available).

Do not treat “related tests only” as sufficient before push unless the user explicitly waives the full suite for that push.
